SDL 3.4.16, D3D12: a draw or dispatch checks that its descriptor tables fit the current GPU heaps
before writing them, and takes new heaps when they do not. Without it, a table written when
fewer slots are left than it has descriptors runs past the heap's end (WriteGPUDescriptors
moves to new heaps only once the index has reached the end exactly), which crashed Hyperion
in the driver with Remastered art on and a few hundred sprites in view (2026-10-15).
Applied by tools/build_sdl3.py.

--- a/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c
+++ b/src/gpu/d3d12/SDL_gpu_d3d12.c
@@ -5068,6 +5068,21 @@
     }
 }
 
+/* Whether the current GPU heaps have room for this many more view and sampler descriptors.
+ * WriteGPUDescriptors only moves to new heaps once the index has reached the end, so a table
+ * written when fewer slots are left than it has descriptors runs past the heap; a draw or a
+ * dispatch checks first, for every table it may write, and takes new heaps when they do not fit. */
+static bool D3D12_INTERNAL_HasDescriptorRoom(
+    D3D12CommandBuffer *commandBuffer,
+    Uint32 viewCount,
+    Uint32 samplerCount)
+{
+    D3D12DescriptorHeap *viewHeap = commandBuffer->gpuDescriptorHeaps[D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_HEAP_TYPE_CBV_SRV_UAV];
+    D3D12DescriptorHeap *samplerHeap = commandBuffer->gpuDescriptorHeaps[D3D12_DESCRIPTOR_HEAP_TYPE_SAMPLER];
+    return viewHeap->currentDescriptorIndex + viewCount <= viewHeap->maxDescriptors &&
+           samplerHeap->currentDescriptorIndex + samplerCount <= samplerHeap->maxDescriptors;
+}
